from pathlib import Path
import base64,json
p=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
clips={k:'data:video/mp4;base64,'+base64.b64encode((p/f'revised-{k}-comparison.mp4').read_bytes()).decode() for k in ['step','push_side']}
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Phone biped V2 · Lower effort, better balance</title><style>
*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#eef0e9;color:#26362c;font:15px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:1180px;margin:auto;padding:40px 24px}small{font:11px ui-monospace,monospace;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#60735f}h1{font-size:clamp(32px,5vw,52px);line-height:1.07;letter-spacing:-.055em;margin:14px 0}header p{max-width:750px;color:#61725d}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:14px;margin:28px 0}.card,.metric{background:#fafbf5;border:1px solid #cfd8c9;border-radius:13px;padding:24px}.metric strong{display:block;font-size:36px;letter-spacing:-.05em;line-height:1.2}.metric small{font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.02em}.metric p{font-size:12px;color:#62745e;margin:8px 0 0}.tabs{display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:20px 0 12px}button{padding:11px 16px;border:1px solid #bdcbb6;border-radius:8px;background:transparent;font:13px system-ui;color:#304c34;cursor:pointer}button[aria-pressed=true]{background:#294432;color:#fff}button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #708f65;outline-offset:3px}.player{padding:8px;background:#121d17;border-radius:16px}video{display:block;width:100%;border-radius:9px}.player p{font:11px ui-monospace,monospace;color:#bfd1b7;padding:0 12px}.columns{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:16px;margin-top:18px}h2{font-size:24px;letter-spacing:-.035em;line-height:1.25;margin:8px 0 14px}.card p,.card li{font-size:13px;color:#5b7055}.card ul{padding-left:18px}.card li{margin:8px 0}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px}td,th{text-align:left;padding:10px 5px;border-bottom:1px solid #dce3d6}th{font-weight:500;color:#667d5d}.wide{margin-top:18px}.callout{border-left:3px solid #6b855b;padding-left:15px;color:#4b6645}footer{font-size:11px;color:#6e8065;margin-top:25px}a{color:inherit}.note{color:#718269;font-size:11px}@media(max-width:650px){main{padding:25px 14px}.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:10px}.metric{padding:16px;display:grid;grid-template-columns:80px 1fr;gap:3px 12px}.metric strong{grid-row:span 2}.metric p{margin:0}.columns{grid-template-columns:1fr}.card{padding:20px}}
</style></head><body><main><header><small>Product design / revision 02 / simulated comparison</small><h1>Lower the phone.<br>Let the feet do more.</h1><p>A more compact biped with a landscape phone mount, shorter legs, a lower battery and broader feet. Modest body-angle feedback improves its balance. We retained all 14 actuated axes.</p></header>
<div class="grid"><div class="metric"><strong>15%</strong><small>Less positive motor work</small><p>For the same first 10 cm of simulated travel: 5.23 → 4.44 J.</p></div><div class="metric"><strong>23 mm</strong><small>Lower centre of mass</small><p>169 → 146 mm above the floor in the initial pose.</p></div><div class="metric"><strong>20%</strong><small>Lower torque-squared integral</small><p>For the same 10 cm task: 3.35 → 2.69 Nm²s, a motor-heating proxy.</p></div></div>
<p class="callout">These are improvements in simulated actuator effort, not measured battery savings. Both designs still use an early shuffling controller with substantial foot slip.</p>
<div class="tabs" role="group" aria-label="Compare design tests"><button data-case="step" aria-pressed="true">Compare movement</button><button data-case="push_side" aria-pressed="false">Compare sideways push</button><button id="slow" aria-pressed="false">¼-speed replay</button></div>
<section class="player"><video id="video" controls playsinline preload="metadata" aria-label="Side by side original and compact robot simulations"></video><p>Left: original · Right: revised · actual MuJoCo state recordings · 12 N push for 160 ms in the push test</p></section>
<section class="card wide"><small>Hardware changes</small><h2>The revised proportions.</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Original</th><th>Recommended V2</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Phone orientation</td><td>Portrait</td><td>Landscape, nearer pelvis</td></tr><tr><td>Thigh / shin length</td><td>80 / 80 mm</td><td>70 / 70 mm</td></tr><tr><td>Each sole</td><td>96 × 60 mm</td><td>120 × 72 mm</td></tr><tr><td>Foot-centre spacing</td><td>106 mm</td><td>118 mm</td></tr><tr><td>Battery centre</td><td>At pelvis origin</td><td>12 mm lower; narrower pack</td></tr><tr><td>Total assumed mass</td><td>1.691 kg</td><td>1.659 kg</td></tr><tr><td>Overall height</td><td>367 mm</td><td>277 mm</td></tr><tr><td>Body-angle feedback</td><td>None</td><td>Ideal pitch/roll feedback to ankles</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The larger feet add model mass; lighter, shorter link targets offset that increase. The revised pack proxy has approximately the same volume. Structural stiffness, real pack packaging, phone retention and full joint clearance still need CAD validation.</p></section>
<div class="columns"><section class="card"><small>Same task / same distance</small><h2>Measure work, not just time.</h2><table><thead><tr><th>First 10 cm</th><th>Original</th><th>V2</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Time from start</td><td>6.03 s</td><td>5.50 s</td></tr><tr><td>Positive motor work</td><td>5.23 J</td><td>4.44 J</td></tr><tr><td>Torque-squared integral</td><td>3.35 Nm²s</td><td>2.69 Nm²s</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The one-second standing setup is excluded from effort totals. No stopping or final settling phase is included. Positive motor work integrates max(torque × joint speed, 0) across all actuators; it does not include electrical losses or credit regenerative braking.</p><p>Torque-squared integral compares heating tendency for unchanged motor/gear families. It is not electrical energy. Battery Wh and runtime need motor constants, winding resistance, gear efficiency, driver losses, phone and controller power.</p></section>
<section class="card"><small>Balance / honest boundaries</small><h2>Better sideways. Forward recovery remains.</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Six-second test</th><th>Original</th><th>V2</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Movement, max tilt</td><td>1.80°</td><td>1.36°</td></tr><tr><td>Side push, max tilt</td><td>106.7°, falls</td><td>19.9°, no fall</td></tr><tr><td>Forward push</td><td>Falls at 2.236 s</td><td>Falls at 2.266 s</td></tr><tr><td>Peak joint torque in movement</td><td>0.76 Nm</td><td>0.82 Nm</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The same 12 N, 160 ms disturbance starts at t = 2 s. Body pitch/roll are read directly from the simulation, without sensor noise or latency. Larger feet and a lower body improve this test, but a recovery-step strategy is still needed for the forward push.</p><p>Peak torque rises about 8% during movement. Retain the assumed motor torque limits for now; lower total effort does not mean smaller peak-capacity motors.</p></section>
<section class="card"><small>Power-saving product behaviour</small><h2>Spend energy when it helps.</h2><ul><li>Turn only the phone toward a person before rotating the whole body. Remain stationary when movement is unnecessary.</li><li>Use a deliberate parking mode. A mechanical support or verified locking mechanism could allow reduced drive current; this hardware is proposed, not simulated.</li><li>Balance the phone cradle around its tilt axis to reduce holding load. Validate every supported phone and case.</li><li>Throttle perception and radio activity when idle while maintaining local balance and fault monitoring. Measure whole-device draw before estimating runtime.</li></ul><p>A small knee spring was explored in the parameter sweep but is not part of this recommendation. Smaller-amplitude steps also proved worse in work per metre in several tested cases. Neither change should be assumed to save energy automatically.</p></section>
<section class="card"><small>Validation performed</small><h2>Promising, still a prototype.</h2><ul><li>Halving the timestep preserves the benefit: about 13.5% less work for the first 10 cm. The lateral-push test still does not fall.</li><li>The revised stepping test stays upright for 20 seconds. A 350 g phone case also stays upright in the six-second test.</li><li>The no-feedback hardware revision alone reduces six-second work per metre by approximately 11%; feedback provides an additional change.</li><li>Self-collision remains disabled; floor contact and friction are simulated. Motors remain ideal torque-limited position servos.</li></ul><p>Sliding is substantial in both designs. The six-second summed contact slip-path metric is 0.36 m for the original and 0.39 m for V2, across both feet; it is not travel distance. A proper lift-and-place gait is the next development step.</p></section></div>
<footer>Model, controller and results: <a href="improve_design.py">design comparison script</a> · <a href="v2-step-model.xml">revised model</a> · <a href="revised-design-results.json">test results</a> · <a href="revised-design-checks.json">checks</a> · <a href="REVISED-DESIGN.md">design notes</a>.<br>Background: <a href="https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/computation/">MuJoCo dynamics</a> · <a href="https://support.maxongroup.com/hc/en-us/articles/360013761160-Motor-data-and-simulation">motor torque and loss relationships</a> · <a href="https://underactuated.mit.edu/simple_legs.html">walking energetics</a>.</footer>
</main><script>const clips=CLIPS;const video=document.querySelector('#video');document.querySelectorAll('[data-case]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{document.querySelectorAll('[data-case]').forEach(x=>x.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(x===b)));video.src=clips[b.dataset.case];video.load();video.play().catch(()=>{})});document.querySelector('#slow').onclick=e=>{const slow=video.playbackRate===1;video.playbackRate=slow?.25:1;e.target.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(slow));e.target.textContent=slow?'Normal speed':'¼-speed replay'};video.src=clips.step;</script></body></html>'''
(p/'phone-biped-v2.html').write_text(html.replace('CLIPS',json.dumps(clips)),encoding='utf-8')
